WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.710
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:09.907
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.207 --> 00:00:16.621
Unit twenty-two: Possessive Pronouns. Today you will say who something belongs to without repeating the noun.

4
00:00:16.921 --> 00:00:19.748
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.026
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:25.745
Mine.

7
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.471
Mine means belonging to me.

8
00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:30.502
The red pen is mine.

9
00:00:31.117 --> 00:00:33.421
Your turn. Say: Mine.

10
00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:37.152
Mine.

11
00:00:37.917 --> 00:00:38.941
Yours.

12
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.775
Yours means belonging to you.

13
00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:43.849
Is this bag yours?

14
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.824
Your turn. Say: Yours.

15
00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:50.621
Yours.

16
00:00:51.383 --> 00:00:52.326
His.

17
00:00:53.317 --> 00:00:54.910
His means belonging to him.

18
00:00:55.517 --> 00:00:56.843
The car is his.

19
00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:00.068
Your turn. Say: His.

20
00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:03.749
His.

21
00:01:04.483 --> 00:01:05.252
Hers.

22
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:08.029
Hers means belonging to her.

23
00:01:08.617 --> 00:01:09.920
The book is hers.

24
00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:13.413
Your turn. Say: Hers.

25
00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:17.094
Hers.

26
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:18.747
Ours.

27
00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.575
Ours means belonging to us.

28
00:01:22.183 --> 00:01:23.718
The house is ours.

29
00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.539
Your turn. Say: Ours.

30
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.297
Ours.

31
00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:31.923
Theirs.

32
00:01:32.917 --> 00:01:34.568
Theirs means belonging to them.

33
00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:36.579
The garden is theirs.

34
00:01:37.183 --> 00:01:39.511
Your turn. Say: Theirs.

35
00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:43.286
Theirs.

36
00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:44.900
Whose.

37
00:01:45.917 --> 00:01:48.102
Whose means used to ask about the owner.

38
00:01:48.717 --> 00:01:50.031
Whose pen is this?

39
00:01:50.617 --> 00:01:52.990
Your turn. Say: Whose.

40
00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:56.718
Whose.

41
00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.380
Belong.

42
00:01:59.383 --> 00:02:01.453
Belong means to be owned by someone.

43
00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:03.736
This bag belongs to Sara.

44
00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.480
Your turn. Say: Belong.

45
00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:10.276
Belong.

46
00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:14.787
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.860
Visal, whose pen is this? Is it yours?

48
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:32.047
Yes, it is mine. Mine is a possessive pronoun. It replaces possessive word + noun, so we do not repeat the noun: This is my pen. This pen is mine.

49
00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.755
What are the other forms?

50
00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:49.351
Yours, his, hers, ours and theirs. For example: That book is hers. Their car is old, but ours is new. The possessive adjective is before a noun and the pronoun stands alone.

51
00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:51.799
Is there any trap?

52
00:02:52.883 --> 00:03:06.428
Do not use an apostrophe: yours, not your's. Also notice his is both an adjective and a pronoun: his book, the book is his. And its has no pronoun form in this meaning.

53
00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:08.951
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.817 --> 00:03:15.949
Grammar focus: Possessive pronouns: mine and yours and his and hers and ours and theirs.

55
00:03:16.249 --> 00:03:17.471
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.183 --> 00:03:19.904
This pen is mine (my pen).

57
00:03:20.817 --> 00:03:22.491
That bag is hers (her bag).

58
00:03:23.383 --> 00:03:25.313
Their car is old, but ours is new.

59
00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:34.111
Mine, yours, his, hers, ours and theirs replace possessive word + noun. Never use an apostrophe. Whose asks about the owner.

60
00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:38.303
Be careful! Don't say: This pen is your's.

61
00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.464
Say: This pen is yours.

62
00:03:42.764 --> 00:03:44.438
Do not use an apostrophe.

63
00:03:45.233 --> 00:03:47.862
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:49.772
Whose Is It?.

65
00:03:50.072 --> 00:03:52.411
Whose bag is this? It is hers.

66
00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.073
This pen is mine, but that one is yours.

67
00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.206
Their house is big, but ours is bigger.

68
00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.049
The books on the desk are theirs.

69
00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:05.126
Never write your's with an apostrophe.

70
00:04:06.233 --> 00:04:10.154
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.297
This is my book. It is blank.

72
00:04:13.597 --> 00:04:16.543
A, me. B, mine. C, my.

73
00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.647
The answer is B: mine.

74
00:04:22.783 --> 00:04:25.018
That is her bag. It is blank.

75
00:04:25.318 --> 00:04:28.646
A, hers. B, her's. C, she.

76
00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.223
The answer is A: hers.

77
00:04:35.383 --> 00:04:38.697
Their car is old, but blank is new. (our car)

78
00:04:38.997 --> 00:04:42.094
A, our. B, ours. C, us.

79
00:04:45.633 --> 00:04:47.366
The answer is B: ours.

80
00:04:48.517 --> 00:04:50.168
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:50.468 --> 00:04:55.039
A, The pen is your's.. B, The pen is yours.. C, The pen is yourn..

82
00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.157
The answer is B: The pen is yours..

83
00:05:02.317 --> 00:05:05.233
According to the reading, whose books are on the desk?

84
00:05:05.533 --> 00:05:09.198
A, theirs. B, mine. C, ours.

85
00:05:12.733 --> 00:05:14.791
The answer is A: theirs.

86
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.908
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:22.040
Point to three things and say who they belong to.

88
00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.408
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:32.708 --> 00:05:44.814
That pen is mine, that bag is hers and those notebooks are theirs. I use possessive pronouns so I do not repeat the noun. Whose is the question word that I use to ask about the owner.

90
00:05:45.114 --> 00:05:46.986
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:47.883 --> 00:05:55.052
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and possessive pronouns: mine and yours and his and hers and ours and theirs.

92
00:05:55.352 --> 00:05:58.933
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

93
00:05:59.233 --> 00:06:02.547
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:06:02.847 --> 00:06:05.767
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

